{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/122982","id":4392916348,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABBdaVfA","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122982","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122982.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122982.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122982","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/122982/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/122982/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122982/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/3a23a4d31460257460c612a9657873ad8edaace6","number":122982,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"Fix audio muting in AnimationMixer when blending animations","user":{"login":"feeib","id":82524202,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgyNTI0MjAy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/82524202?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/feeib","html_url":"https://github.com/feeib","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/feeib/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/feeib/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/feeib/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/feeib/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/feeib/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/feeib/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/feeib/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/feeib/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/feeib/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## What problem(s) does this PR solve?\r\n\r\nWhen blending animations with audio tracks in a **BlendSpace2D**, the audio volume can become a very small negative number. This happens because of small rounding errors in the blend calculation near the edges of the triangulation. When this negative number is passed to `Math::linear_to_db()`, it produces `NaN`. Because `NaN` spreads to everything it touches in the audio mix, this makes all audio go silent. Calling `AnimationMixer::clear_caches() `fixes it temporarily by rebuilding the audio cache.\r\n\r\n- Closes #109119\r\n\r\n## Additional information\r\n\r\n**AI disclosure:** I used GitHub Copilot while investigating this issue reading through AudioServer/AnimationMixer/AudioStreamPlaybackPolyphonic source, and testing hypotheses about the root cause. \r\nI confirmed the root cause and the fix myself through myown debugging and testing in my own project.","labels":[{"id":73330064,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2NA==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/bug","name":"bug","description":"","color":"ff6055","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":572781997,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw1NzI3ODE5OTc=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:audio","name":"topic:audio","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":2666705648,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNjY2NzA1NjQ4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:animation","name":"topic:animation","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":{"id":8237783,"node_id":"MI_kwDOAO6SJc4AfbLX","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/16","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/milestone/16","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/16/labels","number":16,"state":"open","title":"4.x","description":"Issues and pull requests slated for an undetermined Godot 4 release.","creator":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMz